<%# locals: (type_word:, edit: nil, menu: nil, back: nil, assistant_record: nil) %>
<%# The lane's head for a note, a document and their forms (S3 of
    doc/wissen_als_bahn_plan.md, D4), after tickets/_ticket_header_show: a
    quiet chrome row, then the object's title one step UNDER the page title.
    Where the ticket has its number, the knowledge object has its type word
    in mono ("Notiz", "Datei"): a note has no number, and the word says what
    the lane holds without a second heading beside "Wissen".
    Right: the pencil (writers only), the "···" for the rare and the
    consequential (menu:, an array of Neo::OverflowMenuComponent item kwargs;
    the document passes rename and delete, S3 of doc/dokumentansicht_plan.md,
    the note passes none yet), a divider, the ✕. Everything on ONE rank,
    32x32, frameless, cream-500 at rest (the ticket's action bar).
    back: (the file preview, doc/dateivorschau_plan.md D4) is an unconditional
    way back to the OBJECT, a word at the left where the type word stands,
    visible at every width; a lane-link that takes the preview out of the
    address and loads the object's frame (href: the plain fallback), and hands
    the focus to what opened the preview (focus:).
    Below lg the ✕ steps aside and the way back becomes a WORD, because there
    the lane covers the list and a way back to something visible is not a
    way. It is a real link to the page address without the selection and
    WITH the live query (the frame fetch carries it, list_row_controller), so
    it works on both templates. Not on the mobile page: that one renders its
    own "Listenansicht" above the detail (NeoMobileTicketViewComponent).
    History, versions, download and the danger zone stay in the body.
    assistant_record: (doc/assistent_wissen_kontext_plan.md, step 3) is the
    SAVED note or document this head crowns; the display roots and the preview
    pass it, the forms do not (an unsaved draft is nothing the assistant can
    read). It renders the "Assistent" button of the ticket's action bar in this
    row: on the same rank as the pencil, outside the write-right condition (a
    reader may ask about what they may read), lg only like the ✕ (below that
    breakpoint there is no companion lane), attributes from the one owner of
    the page-to-panel seam (assistant_trigger_attributes, nil = no assistant). %>
<% icon_button = "flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-md text-cream-500 transition-colors hover:bg-cream-200 hover:text-cream-900 focus-visible:bg-cream-200 focus-visible:text-cream-900" %>
<% assistant = assistant_record && assistant_trigger_attributes(assistant_record) %>
<% back_query = request.query_parameters.except('frame', 'frame_id', 'format', *knowledge_lane_state_params) %>
<div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-2" data-lane-head>
  <% if back %>
    <a href="<%= back[:href] %>"
       data-lane-back-to-object
       data-controller="lane-link"
       data-lane-link-url-value="<%= back[:url] %>"
       data-lane-link-frame-value="<%= back[:frame] %>"
       data-lane-link-remove-value="<%= back[:remove].to_json %>"
       data-lane-link-focus-value="<%= back[:focus] %>"
       data-action="click->lane-link#click"
       autofocus
       class="inline-flex h-8 items-center gap-1 rounded-lg px-2 -ml-2 text-[13px] font-normal text-cream-600 transition-colors hover:bg-cream-100 hover:text-cream-900 focus-visible:bg-cream-100 focus-visible:text-cream-900">
      <span aria-hidden="true">&lsaquo;</span>
      <%= back[:label] %>
    </a>
  <% else %>
  <span class="hidden lg:inline font-mono text-[13px] tracking-wide text-cream-500"><%= type_word %></span>
  <% end %>

  <% unless @viewport_mode == 'mobile' || back %>
    <a href="<%= organisation_project_knowledge_index_path(@current_organisation, @project, back_query) %>"
       data-lane-back
       data-turbo-frame="_top"
       class="inline-flex lg:hidden h-8 items-center gap-1 rounded-lg px-2 -ml-2 text-[13px] font-normal text-cream-600 transition-colors hover:bg-cream-100 hover:text-cream-900 focus-visible:bg-cream-100 focus-visible:text-cream-900">
      <span aria-hidden="true">&lsaquo;</span>
      <%= t('views.organisations.knowledge.lane.back_to_list') %>
    </a>
  <% end %>

  <div class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-1">
    <% if edit %>
      <a href="<%= edit[:href] %>"
         class="<%= edit[:hook] %> <%= icon_button %>"
         title="<%= edit[:title] %>"
         data-turbo-frame="<%= edit[:frame] %>">
        <i class="bi bi-pencil"></i>
      </a>
    <% end %>
    <% if menu.present? %>
      <%= render Neo::OverflowMenuComponent.new do |overflow| %>
        <% menu.each { |item| overflow.with_item(**item) } %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
    <% if assistant %>
      <%# Icon-only like the ticket's; the title says what it does and, for a
          document, that the CURRENT version is what the assistant reads,
          whatever version the preview shows. %>
      <button type="button"
              class="hidden lg:<%= icon_button %>"
              title="<%= t("views.organisations.knowledge.lane.ask_assistant.#{assistant_record.class.name.underscore}") %>"
              data-lane-assistant
              <%= assistant %>>
        <i class="bi bi-stars"></i>
      </button>
    <% end %>
    <% if edit || menu.present? || assistant %>
      <span class="hidden lg:block h-5 w-px bg-cream-300" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <% end %>
    <button type="button"
            class="hidden lg:flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-md text-cream-500 transition-colors hover:bg-cream-200 hover:text-cream-900 focus-visible:bg-cream-200 focus-visible:text-cream-900"
            title="<%= t('views.organisations.knowledge.lane.close') %>"
            data-lane-close
            data-action="click->layout-toggle#closeContent">
      <i class="bi bi-x-lg"></i>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
